IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Exemption from sections 33, 34(1)(b) and 35) Notification (Cap. 323, N 1),
-- made by the Minister under section 73 of the Telecommunications Act (section 96 in the 2020 Revised Edition).
-- Texts used (all fetched from IMDA's listing page, see subjects/sg/telecommunications-exemption-notification-2001/):
--   the 2002 Revised Edition text (raw id n1), and the amending notifications S 591/2003, S 651/2004, S 265/2006,
--   S 1/2008, S 179/2011, S 252/2013, S 415/2014 and S 726/2014 (raw ids n1s591 ... n1s726).
-- The "sections 33, 34(1)(b) and 35" of the title are the 2000 Revised Edition numbers of what are ss 53, 54(1)(b)
-- and 55 in the 2020 Revised Edition (margin markers in TA1999.txt).
--
-- WHAT IS MODELLED: the operative paragraph 2 in its two forms, and the TITLES of the equipment each Schedule names,
-- in six vintages (the title sets change on 17 October 2001, 2 January 2008, 1 November 2014 and 1 April 2017 and are
-- the same in between; the other amendments change frequency bands and power limits of transmitters, which the bands module
-- sgta-i-n1-bands.l4 models).  A vintage is a function of the date:
--   before 2 March 2001 -> NOTHING.  The Notification as made, S 115/2001, came into operation on 2 March 2001 (TA1999-N1-S115-2001.txt:30-32).
--   2 March 2001 to 16 October 2001: the Notification as made (15 items, in-building or localised on-site; 20 entries, with item 11's six sub-items counted separately).
--   17 October 2001 to 31 December 2002: the Schedule substituted by S 525/2001; the same 21 entries as the 2002 Revised Edition.
--   1 January 2003 to 1 January 2008: the 2002 Revised Edition, which prints the Notification as made and as amended by S 525/2001
--     (its history line, TA1999-N1:166); the PDF does not print the date the Revised Edition began, so 1 January 2003 is assumed (NOTES.md Fork B).
--   2 January 2008 to 31 October 2014, 1 November 2014 to 31 March 2017, 1 April 2017 to 31 August 2023, 1 September 2023 onwards (S 588/2023, added 2026-11-04 from the follow-up list).
-- The last amendment known is S 588/2023 (first published 28 August 2023, in operation 1 September 2023); the Gazette copy of every amendment on IMDA's list is deposited, and S 115/2001 (as made), S 525/2001, S 78/2017 and S 588/2023 are four
-- the e-Gazette supplied that IMDA's list lacks.  Neither list is guaranteed complete, so a later amendment, if there is one, is not known to this encoding.

§ `N 1 paragraph 2: the exemption`

-- src:TA1999-N1:24 | 2. Sections 33, 34 (1) (b) and 35 of the Act shall not apply to any person in respect of —
-- src:TA1999-N1:25 | (a) the possession, establishment, installation, maintenance, provision or operation
-- src:TA1999-N1:26 | of any network or station as defined in the Telecommunications (Radio-
-- src:TA1999-N1:27 | communication) Regulations (Rg 5) where the person has been permitted by the
-- src:TA1999-N1:28 | Authority to use any radio frequency band in respect of the network or station
-- src:TA1999-N1:29 | under regulation 75 of those Regulations; and
-- src:TA1999-N1:30 | (b) the localised on-site installation or operation of the equipment specified in the
-- src:TA1999-N1:31 | Schedule.
@ref N 1 para 2, 2002 Revised Edition (src:TA1999-N1:24-31)
GIVEN `has been permitted by the Authority to use a radio frequency band under regulation 75 of Rg 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the installation or operation is localised and on-site` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is one of those the Schedule specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 2 (2002 Revised Edition form): sections 33, 34(1)(b) and 35 do not apply` MEANS
        `has been permitted by the Authority to use a radio frequency band under regulation 75 of Rg 5`
    OR (`the installation or operation is localised and on-site` AND `the equipment is one of those the Schedule specifies`)

-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:23 | 2. Paragraph 2 of the Telecommunications (Exemption from
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:24 | sections 33, 34(1)(b) and 35) Notification (N 1) is amended —
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:25 | (a) by deleting the word “and” at the end of sub-paragraph (a);
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:26 | (b) by deleting the words “the Schedule” in sub-paragraph (b)
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:27 | and substituting the words “the First Schedule”; and
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:28 | (c) by deleting the full-stop at the end of sub-paragraph (b) and
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:29 | substituting a semi-colon, and by inserting immediately
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:30 | thereafter the following sub-paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:31 | “(c) the installation of an equipment specified in the
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:32 | Second Schedule, where the installation is in
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:33 | accordance with the technical specifications on
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:34 | white space devices published by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:35 | at http://www.ida.gov.sg; and
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:36 | (d) the operation of an equipment specified in the
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:37 | Second Schedule, where the operation is in
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:38 | accordance with the technical specifications on
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:39 | 2
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:42 | white space devices published by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:43 | at http://www.ida.gov.sg.”.
@ref N 1 para 2 as amended by S 726/2014 (src:TA1999-N1-S726-2014:23-43)
GIVEN `has been permitted by the Authority to use a radio frequency band under regulation 75 of Rg 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the installation or operation is localised and on-site` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is one of those the First Schedule specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is one of those the Second Schedule specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the installation or operation is in accordance with the technical specifications on white space devices published by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 2 (form from 1 November 2014): sections 33, 34(1)(b) and 35 do not apply` MEANS
        `has been permitted by the Authority to use a radio frequency band under regulation 75 of Rg 5`
    OR (`the installation or operation is localised and on-site` AND `the equipment is one of those the First Schedule specifies`)
    OR (`the equipment is one of those the Second Schedule specifies` AND `the installation or operation is in accordance with the technical specifications on white space devices published by the Authority`)

