       , `Medical and Biological Telemetry Devices`
       , `Wireless Modem`
       , `Radio Telemetry Equipment`
       , `Remote Control Devices (a) Garage Door Openers`
       , `Remote Control Devices (b) Cameras`
       , `Remote Control Devices (c) Toys and Robots`
       , `Remote Control Devices (d) Battery-operated Cars and Boats`
       , `Remote Control Devices (e) TV Receivers or Radio Systems`
       , `Remote Control Devices (f) Other Miscellaneous Remote Control Devices`
       , `Cordless Telephones or Wireless PABX`
       , `Wireless LAN or Low Power Devices`
       , `Stand-alone GPS Receivers`
       , `Communication Receivers (excluding Scanning devices) and MMDS Receivers`

-- S 525/2001 (in operation 17 October 2001) amends paragraph 2(b) of the Notification of 2001 (S 115/2001, deposited above) by deleting the words "in-building or", and deletes
-- the Schedule and substitutes one of 16 items.
-- The Revised Edition (2002) prints no amendment after S 525/2001 and its history line reads "[G.N. Nos. S115/2001;S 525/2001]" (TA1999-N1:166), so the 2002
-- Revised Edition is the Notification as made and as amended once.  The two Schedules were compared on 2026-11-04 as sequences of words and figures
-- with the headings, page furniture and punctuation set aside: they carry the same 16 items with the same bands and limits.  The only difference is
-- how item 7's four sub-items wrap across the page, and the footnote is word for word the same.  So from 17 October 2001 the items the Schedule
-- names are the Revised Edition's 21 entries (16 numbered items; item 11 has sub-items (a) to (f), counted here as six entries, one of which is
-- 11(e) "TV Receivers/ Radio Systems", S 525/2001 line 114).  The as-made Schedule (above) has the same entries except item 16.
